---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy — Digital Forloop" description="Privacy policy for Digital Forloop apps.">
  <article class="privacy">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: 16 November 2026</p>

    <p>This policy explains what information our mobile games collect, why, who receives it, how long it is kept, and the choices and rights you have. It applies to Pixel Soccer Manager and any other game we publish that links to it (the "Apps").</p>

    <p>The Apps are provided by <strong>Digital Forloop Limited</strong>, a company registered in England and Wales (company number 15958356), whose registered office is at 71-75 Shelton Street, Covent Garden, London WC2H 9JQ, United Kingdom ("we", "us", "our"). We are the data controller for the information described here, under the UK General Data Protection Regulation (UK GDPR) and the Data Protection Act 2018. We are registered with the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO) under number ZB804207.</p>

    <p>If you have any question about this policy or your information, email us at <a href="mailto:contact@digitalforloop.com">contact@digitalforloop.com</a>.</p>

    <section>
      <h2>1. Summary</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>You do not create an account to play, and we do not ask for your name, email address, phone number, contacts, photos or precise location.</li>
        <li>Your game progress, in-game currency and settings are saved on your device only.</li>
        <li>Some information is collected automatically and is linked to identifiers for your device and installation, such as an advertising ID. Under data protection law this is personal data, and this policy treats it that way.</li>
        <li>On first launch the game asks for your year of birth. If you are under 16, analytics and personalised adverts stay off and can't be switched on.</li>
        <li>If you are 16 or over, the game then asks for your choices on its Privacy Settings screen. Analytics and personalised adverts are off unless you switch them on, and you can change your mind at any time in Settings › GDPR.</li>
        <li>On iPhone and iPad, players aged 16 or over also see Apple's tracking prompt, which asks whether we may track you. Personalised adverts are shown only if you allow it there too.</li>
        <li>Crash reports are collected whatever you choose, because we need them to keep the game working.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>

      <h3>Identifiers</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Advertising ID</strong>: Apple's Identifier for Advertising (IDFA) on iOS, only if you allow tracking in Apple's prompt, and Google's Android Advertising ID on Android, unless you have deleted or reset it in your device settings. Our advertising partner Unity uses it.</li>
        <li><strong>Installation identifiers</strong>: a random ID the game creates when it is first opened, which we use as your analytics user ID; the Firebase installation and app-instance IDs; and an anonymous customer ID created by RevenueCat, our purchase-management provider. None of these contain your name or contact details.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>How you use the game</h3>
      <p>When analytics is switched on, we collect which screens and features you use, when sessions start and how long they last, in-game events such as matches played, rewards collected and shop items viewed, and your Privacy Settings choices. With it we receive the device model, operating system, language, app version and a broad device performance tier.</p>

      <h3>Purchases and subscriptions</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>When you buy in-game currency or a subscription, Apple or Google take the payment. We never receive your card or bank details.</li>
        <li>We and RevenueCat receive what was bought, its price and currency, the transaction and order identifiers, and, for a subscription, its status, renewal date and expiry date.</li>
        <li>We use this to give you what you paid for, to restore subscriptions, and to keep financial records.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Crash and performance data</h3>
      <p>If the game crashes or hits a serious error, Firebase Crashlytics sends a crash report. It contains the error, the state of the app at the time, the device model, operating system, free memory and disk space, and the installation identifiers above.</p>

      <h3>Advertising data</h3>
      <p>Our Apps show adverts from Unity Ads, which may be delivered through Unity LevelPlay, Unity's ad mediation service. Unity receives:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>the adverts shown to you and how you interact with them, such as views, clicks and whether you watched a rewarded advert to the end;</li>
        <li>your device's language, make, model, screen size and connection type;</li>
        <li>your IP address, from which an approximate location (country or region) is worked out;</li>
        <li>if you report an advert, the report you send.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Unity uses the advertising ID only when personalised adverts are allowed (see section 4).</p>

      <h3>Time checks</h3>
      <p>To keep in-game time fair, the game reads the current time from public web servers (Google and Cloudflare). Those servers receive your IP address, as with any web request. No other information is sent.</p>

      <h3>Names you type into the game</h3>
      <p>Club, manager and player names you enter are checked on your device for offensive words and saved on your device. They are not sent to us.</p>

      <h3>If you contact us</h3>
      <p>If you email us or message us on our Discord server, we receive your email address or username and whatever you write.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>3. How we use it, and our legal grounds</h2>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Purpose</th><th>Information used</th><th>Legal ground (UK GDPR)</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Running the game, saving your progress on your device, delivering purchases and subscription benefits, restoring subscriptions</td><td>Purchase and subscription data, installation identifiers</td><td>Contract: we need it to provide what you asked for</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Fixing crashes and keeping the game stable</td><td>Crash and performance data</td><td>Legitimate interests: keeping the game working for everyone</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Analytics: understanding how the game is played so we can improve it</td><td>Usage data, installation identifiers</td><td>Consent, which you give or refuse on the Privacy Settings screen</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Non-personalised adverts, which pay for the free game</td><td>Advertising data, without the advertising ID</td><td>Legitimate interests: funding a free game</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Personalised adverts, matched to your interests</td><td>Advertising data, including the advertising ID</td><td>Consent: the Privacy Settings screen, and on iOS also Apple's tracking prompt</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Remote settings, such as prices, events and game balance, without updating the app</td><td>Installation identifiers, app version, device data</td><td>Legitimate interests: running and balancing the game</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Checking the time</td><td>IP address</td><td>Legitimate interests: preventing clock manipulation</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Preventing fraud and validating purchases</td><td>Purchase data, installation identifiers</td><td>Legitimate interests, and contract</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Answering your messages</td><td>Your email or username and message</td><td>Legitimate interests: helping you</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Keeping financial and tax records</td><td>Purchase data</td><td>Legal obligation</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>We do not sell your information, and we do not use it to make decisions about you that have legal or similarly significant effects.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>4. Your choices</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Privacy Settings screen.</strong> It appears the first time you open the game, and again from Settings › GDPR. Analytics and personalised adverts are each off until you switch them on. You can withdraw consent at any time on the same screen. Withdrawing doesn't affect what was collected before.</li>
        <li><strong>Apple's tracking prompt (iPhone and iPad).</strong> After you save your Privacy Settings, iOS asks whether the game may track you. You can change the answer at any time in your device's Settings › Privacy &amp; Security › Tracking. Adverts are personalised only if you allow both this prompt and personalised adverts in Privacy Settings.</li>
        <li><strong>Android advertising ID.</strong> You can delete or reset it in your device's Settings › Privacy › Ads, or Settings › Google › Ads on some devices.</li>
        <li><strong>Adverts.</strong> With personalised adverts off you still see adverts, but they are not based on your interests. The Remove Adverts subscription removes pop-up adverts between screens. Adverts you choose to watch for a reward stay available.</li>
        <li><strong>Deleting the game.</strong> Uninstalling the App deletes everything it stored on your device: your progress, settings and installation identifier. It does not cancel a subscription; cancel that in your App Store or Google Play account.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>5. Who receives your information</h2>
      <p>We share information only with the providers who run parts of the game for us, and only for the purposes above. Our data processors act only on our instructions, under data processing terms that require them to protect it. They are:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Google LLC (Firebase Analytics, Firebase Crashlytics, Firebase Remote Config), our data processor.</strong> Google processes analytics, crash and configuration data on our behalf. Privacy: <a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://policies.google.com/privacy</a></li>
        <li><strong>Unity Technologies (Unity Ads, and Unity LevelPlay where used).</strong> Unity serves adverts and measures them. For personalised adverts, Unity also uses the data for its own advertising purposes, as an independent controller, under its own policy: <a href="https://unity.com/legal/game-player-and-app-user-privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://unity.com/legal/game-player-and-app-user-privacy-policy</a></li>
        <li><strong>RevenueCat, Inc., our data processor.</strong> It validates and manages purchases and subscriptions on our behalf. Privacy: <a href="https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy</a></li>
        <li><strong>Apple and Google</strong>, as the app stores that sell the Apps and take payment, under their own privacy policies.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We may also disclose information:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>if the law requires it, or a court or regulator orders it;</li>
        <li>to protect the rights, property or safety of our players, us or others, including to prevent fraud;</li>
        <li>to a buyer or successor if our business or an App is sold or reorganised, who must then use it as this policy describes.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Links in the game to other services, such as our Discord server, YouTube channel or the app stores, are covered by those services' own policies.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>6. International transfers</h2>
      <p>Google, Unity and RevenueCat are based in, or process data in, the United States and other countries outside the UK. Where information is transferred out of the UK, we rely on one of these safeguards:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>the UK Extension to the EU-US Data Privacy Framework, where the provider is certified;</li>
        <li>the International Data Transfer Agreement, or the UK Addendum to the EU Standard Contractual Clauses, approved under UK law.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>You can ask us for details of the safeguards.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>7. How long we keep it</h2>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Information</th><th>How long</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Game progress, settings and identifiers on your device</td><td>Until you delete the App or clear its data</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Analytics data (Firebase Analytics)</td><td>Up to 14 months, then deleted. Reports that cannot identify you may be kept longer</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Crash reports (Firebase Crashlytics)</td><td>90 days</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Purchase and subscription records (RevenueCat, and our own financial records)</td><td>As long as the subscription is active, and then up to 6 years for tax and accounting</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Advertising data (Unity Ads)</td><td>As set out in Unity's privacy policy</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Your messages to us</td><td>Up to 2 years after the conversation ends</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under UK data protection law you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>ask for a copy of the personal data we hold about you;</li>
        <li>ask us to correct it or delete it;</li>
        <li>object to our use of it where we rely on legitimate interests, or ask us to restrict it;</li>
        <li>receive it in a portable format;</li>
        <li>withdraw consent at any time, using the choices in section 4.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>To exercise any of these rights, email <a href="mailto:contact@digitalforloop.com">contact@digitalforloop.com</a>. Because we don't hold your name or email address, we can only find data linked to your device if you help us identify it. For purchase data, include the order number from your App Store or Google Play receipt. For other data, tell us your device model and roughly when you installed the game. We will tell you if we need anything else. We respond within one month.</p>
      <p>If you are unhappy with how we have handled your information, you can complain to the Information Commissioner's Office:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>online at <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint</a></li>
        <li>by phone on 0303 123 1113</li>
        <li>by post to Information Commissioner's Office, Wycliffe House, Water Lane, Wilmslow, Cheshire, SK9 5AF.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We'd appreciate the chance to deal with your concern first.</p>

      <h3>If you live in the European Union</h3>
      <p>You have the same rights under the EU General Data Protection Regulation, and you can also complain to the data protection authority in the country where you live.</p>

      <h3>If you live in the United States</h3>
      <p>Some US states, including California, give residents rights over their personal information: to know what is collected, to have it deleted or corrected, and to opt out of its "sale" or "sharing" for targeted advertising. We do not sell personal information for money. When personalised adverts are on, advertising data is shared with Unity for targeted advertising. You can opt out at any time by switching personalised adverts off in Settings › GDPR, or by not allowing tracking on iOS. To use your other rights, email <a href="mailto:contact@digitalforloop.com">contact@digitalforloop.com</a>. We will not treat you differently for using them.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>9. Children</h2>
      <p>The Apps are intended for players aged 13 and over and are not directed at children under 13. If you are under 13, please don't use the Apps. If we learn that we hold information from a child under 13, we will delete it.</p>
      <p>The game asks for your year of birth when it first opens. It keeps only the year, on your device; we never receive it. If you are under 16, analytics and personalised adverts stay off and can't be switched on, and on iPhone and iPad you won't be asked about tracking. You will still see non-personalised adverts, and crash reports are still collected. For players aged 16 and 17, both stay off unless switched on in Privacy Settings. We recommend that they make those choices with a parent or guardian.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>10. Security</h2>
      <p>We use the security measures our providers offer. Data sent from the game to them is encrypted in transit, and access to their consoles is limited to the people who need it. No method of storage or transmission is completely secure. If you think information about you has been misused, contact us at <a href="mailto:contact@digitalforloop.com">contact@digitalforloop.com</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>We will update this policy when the Apps or the information they collect change, and change the date at the top. If a change is significant, for example a new kind of information or a new provider, we will tell you in the game before it takes effect. Where consent is needed, we will ask for it again.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>12. Contact us</h2>
      <p>Digital Forloop Limited<br />71-75 Shelton Street, Covent Garden<br />London WC2H 9JQ<br />United Kingdom<br />Email: <a href="mailto:contact@digitalforloop.com">contact@digitalforloop.com</a></p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

